WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.938
How does a gene become RNA?

00:00:02.565 --> 00:00:04.155
Meet RNA polymerase.

00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:06.861
DNA has two strands, but it reads

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:07.592
just one.

00:00:08.219 --> 00:00:10.158
That one is called the template strand.

00:00:10.785 --> 00:00:12.491
First, the DNA opens up.

00:00:12.944 --> 00:00:15.347
Then polymerase builds RNA that matches the

00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:17.239
template, one base at a time.

00:00:17.692 --> 00:00:19.469
Like tracing a drawing by following just

00:00:19.538 --> 00:00:20.177
one line.

00:00:20.804 --> 00:00:23.660
RNA polymerase reads one DNA strand, the

00:00:23.706 --> 00:00:25.773
template strand, to build RNA.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:27.398
So what's the other strand?

00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:28.339
Swipe.
